  "correct": "1",
  "solution": "The logic followed here is : **Square of (1st number - 2nd number) = 3rd number**\n\nGiven :\n\n \n• (16, 7, 81)\n\n​(16 - 7)² = 81\n\n = 81\n\n81 = 81 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• (24, 16, 64)\n\n​(24 - 16)² = 64\n\n(8)² = 64\n\n64 = 64 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (13, 7, 36)\n\n​(13 - 7)² = 36\n\n(6)² = 36\n\n36 = 36 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (2) : (48, 39, 18)\n\n​(48 - 39)² = 18\n\n(9)² = 18\n\n**81 ≠ 18 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (37, 25, 100)\n\n​(37 - 25)² = 100\n\n(12)² = 100\n\n**144 ≠ 100 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (21, 19, 8)\n\n​(21 - 19)² = 8\n\n(2)² = 8\n\n**4 ≠ 8 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\nHence, **\"Option - (1)\"** is the correct answer.\n\n3f:T112e,",
